<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Excludes files that are pure OS/hardware or process interop (Win32 capture, WGC frame pump,
  file/JSON I/O, the named-pipe channel, each exe's entry point) from the coverage gate. These
  have no branching business logic worth pinning with unit tests and can't run without a live
  display or a second process; they're verified manually and via the replay/parity regression
  tests instead. Excluding a file only affects the aggregate percentage, never whether anything
  in it gets tested.

  Everything else stays gated — the contracts, the plugins' parser/state-machine/ledger code, the
  engine's scan loop, subscription registry, gRPC service, OCR pipeline and hotkey parsing, and
  the SDK's tick mapping.

  Carried over from the monolith's tests/TrackingService.Tests/coverlet.runsettings and re-pointed
  at the engine/plugin layout after ENGINE-SPLIT TASK-8 retired src/TrackingService. The list is
  the old one with three deliberate adjustments, each noted because the layout forced a choice:

  - Trackers/TrackerHost.cs and Trackers/FrameDumpTracker.cs are gone with the files. ScanLoop,
    which replaced TrackerHost, is directly tested and therefore stays gated.
  - The former ProbeConfig.cs became Configuration/EngineConfig.cs, still excluded — it is the same
    exists/write-defaults/deserialize body. The plugins' MissionConfig.cs and RefineryConfig.cs
    are NOT excluded despite the same shape: RefineryConfig.ResolveLedgerPath carries the rule
    that keeps a replay from writing into real order history, and LedgerTargetTests pins it.
  - Capture/LiveFrameSource.cs is added: it is the WGC frame pump extracted out of the monolith's
    MonitorCapture path, and like MonitorCapture it cannot run without a live capture session.
  - Tray/TrayApplication.cs and Tray/TrayIconFactory.cs are the in-process tray's STA message loop and
    GDI icon drawing — process/UI edge that cannot run without a desktop. TASK-UI-05 deleted the three
    WinForms dialogs that used to sit alongside them (Tray/StatusForm.cs, Tray/SettingsForm.cs,
    Tray/PluginsForm.cs) once the WebView2 main window and the control API replaced them as the
    engine's interactive surface; nothing takes their place in this list because there is no file left
    to exclude. The tray's actual display decisions live in Tray/TrayViewBuilder.cs,
    Tray/FrameRateTracker.cs and Tray/TrayIconState.cs, which are pure and stay gated
    (TrayViewBuilderTests, FrameRateTrackerTests). Tray/TrayControls.cs is a callback carrier whose only
    consumers are the excluded UI-edge files, so it is excluded too; Tray/EngineSettings.cs carries the
    value-equality the no-op-save guard relies on and stays gated (EngineSettingsTests).
  - Shell/MainWindow.cs (TASK-UI-04, extended by TASK-UI-05 with live theme and folder-picker support)
    joins the same excluded UI-edge set as Tray/TrayApplication.cs: a WinForms Form hosting a WebView2
    control needs a real WebView2 runtime and a desktop to construct at all. Shell/WindowChrome.cs (the
    DwmSetWindowAttribute P/Invoke wrapper) and Shell/SingleInstance.cs (the mutex/event pair) are NOT
    excluded — both factor out cleanly enough to run headless (a best-effort P/Invoke call that must
    never throw; a named-kernel-object handshake) and are directly tested (WindowChromeTests,
    SingleInstanceTests).
  - Plugins/PluginInstaller.cs and Plugins/PluginLauncher.cs are the plugin manager's two remaining
    edges: the one HTTP client in the engine, and child-process start/stop. TASK-UI-05 deleted
    Tray/PluginsForm.cs, the WinForms dialog that used to sit alongside them — its catalog orchestration
    (FetchCatalogAsync/FetchPreviewCatalogAsync/ResolveLatestVersionAsync sequencing) had already moved
    to Hosting/ControlApi.cs under TASK-UI-03. Everything these two decide was pushed out into
    Plugins/PluginCatalog.cs (the trust rules), Plugins/PluginArchive.cs (unpack safety),
    Plugins/ReleaseVersionResolver.cs, Plugins/PluginPaths.cs, Plugins/PluginInstallState.cs and
    Plugins/PluginRowBuilder.cs, all of which are pure and stay gated. That split is the point: the
    rules that keep a download on the plugins repository and inside the plugin folder are testable
    without a network or a desktop. Plugin log capture follows the same split: the ring itself
    (Plugins/PluginLogBuffer.cs, Plugins/PluginLogStore.cs) and the redirect/decode decisions
    (Plugins/PluginProcessCapture.cs) are pure and gated, leaving only the Start/BeginOutputReadLine
    sequencing behind the launcher's exclusion.

  TASK-8's brief also listed Hosting/HotkeyListener.cs and Processing/OcrPipeline.cs as process-edge files
  to exclude. They are deliberately NOT excluded, because the same task moved 28 tests onto their
  pure helpers (ParseHotkey, EffectiveScale, CropAndScale, the language diagnostics). Excluding
  them would hide the most-tested arithmetic in the engine from the gate, which contradicts the
  instruction to keep the previously-gated bar unchanged — the monolith gated both files too.
  They read low (mixed pure helpers plus OS-bound async methods); that is expected, not a gap.

  As before, there is no numeric threshold here: the gate is this exclusion policy, and the bar is
  read off the aggregate.

  Usage (from the repo root): dotnet test against a project, passing this file via the `settings`
  switch and turning on the collector via the `collect` switch with value "XPlat Code Coverage".
  See .github/workflows/ci.yml's "Test with coverage" step for the exact invocation. Deliberately
  not spelled out as a literal command line here: an XML comment cannot contain two adjacent ASCII
  hyphens, and every CLI flag above needs exactly that — a previous version of this comment used
  U+2011 non-breaking hyphens to dodge the rule, which is exactly the kind of thing a retype quietly
  undoes.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <DataCollectionRunSettings>
    <DataCollectors>
      <DataCollector friendlyName="XPlat code coverage">
        <Configuration>
          <Format>cobertura</Format>
          <ExcludeByFile>
            **/Capture/CaptureInterop.cs,
            **/Capture/MonitorCapture.cs,
            **/Capture/LiveFrameSource.cs,
            **/Operations/FrameSaver.cs,
            **/Configuration/EngineConfig.cs,
            **/ConsoleSink.cs,
            **/NamedPipeChannel.cs,
            **/Metrics/MetricsSampler.cs,
            **/Metrics/MetricsReporter.cs,
            **/Tray/TrayApplication.cs,
            **/Tray/TrayControls.cs,
            **/Tray/TrayIconFactory.cs,
            **/Shell/MainWindow.cs,
            **/Plugins/PluginInstaller.cs,
            **/Plugins/PluginLauncher.cs,
            **/Program.cs
          </ExcludeByFile>
        </Configuration>
      </DataCollector>
    </DataCollectors>
  </DataCollectionRunSettings>
</RunSettings>
